# Vue Core Change Surface

When package or private-tool source files are in scope:

- Identify the owning package and any public exports before editing.
- Inspect adjacent `__tests__` files and package READMEs before choosing a test style.
- Use the minimum API needed for a regression test.
- Prefer `@vue/runtime-test` for platform-neutral renderer behavior. Use DOM or other platform runtimes only when platform behavior is under test.
- For compiler changes, inspect both semantic assertions and snapshots. Do not treat snapshot approval alone as proof of correctness.
- For public type or declaration changes, inspect `packages-private/dts-test` and `packages-private/dts-built-test`.
- For DOM, hydration, playground, template explorer, or interaction changes, state whether browser automation and e2e tests are required.
- For runtime changes, consider dev-only guards, tree shaking, bundle size, and hot-path cost.
- Check package manifests when adding non-type imports or re-exporting types.
- If a source change affects public documentation, record that the public docs source is the separate `vuejs/docs` repository unless current project guidance says otherwise.

Do not convert observed pull-request patterns into universal file-pair rules. Do not update snapshots without reviewing the semantic output. Do not add dependencies only because an alias resolves locally.
